  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: HTTP/2 requests without an authority bypassed strict\n     SNI validation - the fix for CVE-2026-32990 required an authority only\n     for CONNECT requests, so a request using any other method could omit it\n     and evade the host check\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-65637.patch: treat a missing serverName as a\n       missing header for all non-CONNECT HTTP/2 requests in\n       receivedEndOfHeaders()\n     - CVE-2026-65637\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Denial of service via an allocation leak in the HTTP/2\n     backlog - resetting a stream that was waiting on the connection window\n     left its reservation counted in the backlog and its allocation\n     unreturned, so repeated resets exhausted the connection window and\n     stalled the connection\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-68763.patch: remove a replaced stream from the\n       backlog and return its unused allocation to the connection window,\n       decrement backLogSize when allocating, and skip streams that can no\n       longer write\n     - CVE-2026-68763",
